course: dictionary
lesson: 7759
title: Purchase, a formal word for buy
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Purchase is a more formal word for buy. You will see it on shop signs, websites and receipts. Context helps you work out its meaning. «A clear family rule about buying, such as one purchase a month, prevents most arguments.» Here a purchase is something you have bought, so it is a noun.
explain: Purchase can also be a verb, meaning to buy. «Never buy coins without a parent's permission» uses buy, and «Never make a purchase online without a parent's permission» uses the more formal noun phrase. Both mean the same idea of spending money on something.
explain: Purchase can even mean a firm hold or grip. «My feet couldn't get a purchase on the ice» is not about buying anything. Check by swapping in buy: «my feet couldn't get a buy on the ice» does not make sense, so this is a different meaning.
fact: Purchase can be a verb (to buy something) or a noun (something you have bought, or the act of buying).
fact: «Purchasing power» is what your money can buy: £5 buys 10 sweets at 50p, but only 9 at 55p, with 5p left.
fact: Check the sum: 10 × 50p = £5, and 9 × 55p = 495p, which leaves 5p.
fact: «Make a purchase», «proof of purchase» and «in-app purchases» are phrases you may see on websites and in games.
fact: Never make a purchase online without a parent's permission, because purchases can cost real money.
exercise: «Purchasing power is what your money can buy.» If sweets cost 50p each, how many can £5 buy? | 9 | *10 | 5 | 50
exercise: «My feet couldn't get a purchase on the ice.» What does purchase mean here? | The price of a sweet | *A firm hold or grip | Something you have bought | To buy something
exercise: Which word is a more formal way to say buy? | pearl | perch | *purchase | pour
test: In «in-app purchases», what is being described? | *Things you buy inside an app or game | Pictures that show how an app looks | Things you find for free in a game | Lessons from school
test: What does «proof of purchase» mean? | A promise to pay later | *Something that shows you bought an item | A list of prices in a shop | A way to test a product before you buy it
exam: Which sentence uses purchase as a noun? | «We are purchasing new bags» | «They purchased a house last year» | *«The bike was a good purchase» | «Please purchase the tickets now»
